WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.990
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:18.630
Last time: odd & even, with pairs of laddoos

3
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:24.950
Chapter 3 · Place Value Power-Up

4
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:36.240
23 and 32: same digits. Same number?

5
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.920
Let's find out at the sweet shop!

6
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:49.040
Mum's note: 23 laddoos

7
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:58.550
3 boxes of ten + 2 loose laddoos

8
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:09.960
Mum counts: 32 laddoos! Too many!

9
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:21.900
Same digits, 2 and 3. What went wrong?

10
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:36.890
23 = 2 tens + 3 ones · 32 = 3 tens + 2 ones

11
00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:46.320
Digits: the ten symbols 0 to 9

12
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.390
Place value: worth, because of WHERE it sits

13
00:01:50.390 --> 00:02:03.540
Right to left: ones · tens · hundreds

14
00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:13.620
In 58, the 8 is in the ones place

15
00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:25.700
10 sticks → 1 bundle = 1 ten

16
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:31.240
4 bundles + 7 sticks = 47

17
00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:40.220
The 4 means 4 tens = 40. The 7 means 7 ones

18
00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:46.230
4 tens + 2 ones = ?

19
00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:50.060
40 + 2 = 42

20
00:02:50.060 --> 00:03:03.230
Swap 47 → 74: 7 tens + 4 ones. Much bigger!

21
00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:12.770
Swap the digits of 61. What do you get?

22
00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:23.740
61 → 16: 1 ten + 6 ones

23
00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:31.680
10 tens = 1 hundred

24
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:37.910
352 = 3 hundreds + 5 tens + 2 ones

25
00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:48.840
The 5 in 352 is worth 50, not 5

26
00:03:48.840 --> 00:04:00.380
Expanded form: 352 = 300 + 50 + 2

27
00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:10.440
Which number is 300 + 40 + 7?

28
00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:19.200
3 hundreds + 4 tens + 7 ones = 347

29
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:26.650
How many tens are in 90?

30
00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:34.260
90 = 9 tens + 0 ones

31
00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:44.580
Zero holds the place. Without it, 90 is just 9

32
00:04:44.580 --> 00:05:00.260
27 pencils + 1 more bundle of ten = ?

33
00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:11.500
3 tens + 7 ones = 37 pencils

34
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:23.980
Chapter 1: binary lights worth 4 · 2 · 1

35
00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:32.080
Binary 100 = 4

36
00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:40.900
Our numbers: 100 = one hundred

37
00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:53.080
×10 or ×2: either way, position matters!

38
00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.960
Your turn: practice check

39
00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:06.350
In 47, what does the 4 stand for?

40
00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:15.700
4 tens = 40. It sits in the tens place!

41
00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:23.030
Places: hundreds · tens · ones

42
00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:25.450
The place tells a digit's value

43
00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:30.320
23 ≠ 32: position matters

44
00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.840
Binary cares about position too

45
00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:37.950
Chapter 3 done!

46
00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:44.750
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
